# evidence-for: FR-013, NFR-002
# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# D-083 - the handler between the skill and the schema it names.
#
# D-071 reconciled schemas/findings.py. This is the HANDLER around it,
# tools/validation.py, which is what the Validate-Report tool actually runs and
# what skills/trace/SKILL.md:255 and skills/prove/SKILL.md:209 instruct every
# stream to call on its own report. It imported SCHEMAS and then re-declared
# two vocabularies by hand, and one of them SYNTHESIZED the abolished severity
# tier, live.
#
# Block 1 replays the retired roll-ups on the report each skill's own findings
# block documents. trace could only ever read by_severity and by_category as
# {"unknown": N}, because neither is a property of the record being counted;
# prove reported zero of everything because it counted a root `verdicts`
# container that PROVE_SCHEMA does not declare. Block 2 is the same two reports
# through the shipped tool: both valid, both recounted on by_classification -
# and the axis is read out of each SKILL.md's own summary block, not typed into
# the handler, which is what makes the agreement a binding rather than a
# coincidence.
#
# Blocks 3 and 4 are the repair, and its direction. The retired _auto_fix
# branch mapped a legacy `category` onto critical/major/minor and stamped the
# result on the finding. Because the finding item is closed and declares no
# severity, that made the report strictly MORE invalid: the additional-property
# error grew from naming ('category', 'line') to naming ('category', 'line',
# 'severity'). It was not dead code - FR-021/AC-026 make pre-change archives a
# supported input, and a pre-change trace report is exactly what carries
# `category`. auto_fix now only ever SUBTRACTS: it drops the keys the schema
# does not declare, names every drop, and leaves the three MISSING required
# fields missing for the validator to name rather than inventing them. The
# string severity occurs nowhere in the result.
#
# Block 5 is the anti-drift pin, and the reason nothing above can regress
# quietly. The schema is handed in through schema_path and its vocabulary -
# widgets, sheds, colour, roof, mood - exists nowhere in this tree, so no
# branch in the handler can special-case it: the containers, the totals, the
# roll-ups and the repair were all derived from the document in front of it.
# by_colour is sourced from widgets and by_roof from sheds, which is the
# axis-to-container resolution the prove branch got wrong. by_mood is declared
# by the summary and sourceable from no container, so it is omitted rather than
# reported as an empty or all-unknown tally. The OPEN container keeps its
# undeclared key; only a container the schema closes is repaired.
#
# Block 6 is temper, the built-in schema with two containers, where by_status
# is a property of a DOMAIN rather than of a finding. Counting `status` over
# `findings` would have produced precisely the {"unknown": N} shape block 1
# shows.

